    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#cattle">cattle</a> kingdom of south-western Uganda ruled by the Hinda dynasty, whose kingship was embodied in the royal drum Bagyendanwa.</li><li>Its society was divided between Bahima herders, who held power, and Bairu farmers, who formed the majority.</li><li>The 1901 Ankole Agreement enlarged it under British rule; it was abolished in 1967 and never restored.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>In Nkore the kingship was embodied in the royal drum Bagyendanwa, which had its own shrine, attendants and herds, and a king's sons traditionally fought one another for the throne.</p></aside>
    </section>

